{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"5520e71620bdfc2ab6815c2abcfcc43b0820b09d15cb8d480493886a13fb5b02","packTokens":2895,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":374,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":695,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1505,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Import procurement and receiving data and map PO lines to lots and pens with traceability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Forecast lifecycle milestones, target weights, and projected market dates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Track feed inventory, stock movements, wastage, and forecasts across multiple time horizons.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Create and optimize rations with ingredient proportions, nutritional values, and costs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Generate pen-level feeding plans and schedules using bunk rates, ration, and animal counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Record feeding activities, compare planned and actual quantities, decrement inventory, and roll up lot costs and consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Record dated lot weight measurements and maintain weight trends.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate feed-to-gain metrics, profitability, forecasts, and recommendations from feeding and weight data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide dashboards, reports, filters, and CSV or PDF exports for feedlot operations and performance.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Create mock data and present the proposed architecture, demo, validation, challenges, readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How should ration cost optimization produce candidate mixes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Generate candidate ingredient proportions against user-entered nutrition or animal-range constraints; show the cost and trade-offs, and require a user to save or assign a candidate.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which user roles and permissions should the app enforce?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use Administrator and Operator roles: administrators manage users, imports, and configuration; operators manage plans and record feeding and weights; both can view dashboards and reports.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users sign in to the app?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use administrator-managed email and password accounts; defer SSO and self-service registration.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"When a PO line is split across multiple lots, how should its purchase costs be allocated to each lot’s financial baseline?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allocate costs in proportion to the received animal head count assigned to each lot.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should wastage appear as its own dated inventory movement, or only as a factor in usage and forecasts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Include wastage in the configured consumption estimate and projections, but do not create a separate wastage movement.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the bunk rate be interpreted when generating a pen’s planned feed quantity?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day, multiplied by the planned animal count.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Should feed-to-gain calculations use feed quantities as-fed or adjust them to dry matter?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use as-fed pounds for feed consumption and FCR.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When a pen contains animals from multiple lots, how should a pen-level feeding plan or activity be attributed for lot rollups?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record a separate lot allocation for each portion of the pen’s planned or delivered feed.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the full 22-requirement scope be approved as one run, split across runs, or reduced?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 22 requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build a responsive Feedlot web app with email-and-password sign-in for administrator-managed accounts, no self-service registration or SSO, and role-based Administrator and Operator account, navigation, and page controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Administrators to synchronize procurement and receiving records from the configured mock source, showing returned fields, source identifiers, per-record outcomes, updates to previously imported records, and errors for failed records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Display procurement traceability from PO lines through lots to pens, available procurement and animal fields, pen capacity and current animal counts, and lot purchase-cost allocations proportional to received head counts; show missing animal sex as Unknown.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Show each lot’s target weight, lifecycle milestones, projected market date, and projection assumption, using measured ADG when available and otherwise the configured yard expected daily gain, with any lot-specific target override.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Support viewing and entering feed inventory fields while retaining entered units, displaying normalized calculation values where applicable, and showing opening, received, consumed, and closing stock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Show inventory estimates for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month, and annual horizons using the configured wastage ratio, without displaying a separate wastage stock movement; show returned receipts and feed consumption movements.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Allow users to create and view rations with ingredient proportions, nutritional values, intended animal or weight range, and calculated cost per pound in normalized calculation units while retaining entered units for display.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Display ration optimization candidate mixes with ingredient proportions, costs, and trade-offs, and save or assign a candidate only after an explicit action is accepted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Generate dated pen feeding plans showing planned quantity calculated from bunk rate and planned animal count, plan details, and separate lot allocations proportional to current lot animal counts in the pen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Show pen feeding schedules by delivery date and pen, with planned quantity and Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Operators to record feeding activities with or without a matching plan, submit activity details and lot allocations, and show returned planned and actual quantities, variance when linked to a plan, inventory result, feed cost, energy, status, lot allocations, and lot rollups; identify unplanned activities and plan mismatches.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"For accepted feeding activities, display inventory consumption and lot allocations returned by the API without asserting a web-side inventory decrement formula.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"If feeding is refused for insufficient stock, retain entered activity values and show the returned error without presenting the activity as saved or showing updated inventory or lot totals.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"For authorized feeding activity edits or cancellations, show the returned activity state and inventory and lot totals, or the returned error and existing activity details if refused.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Operators to record dated lot weight measurements and show returned measurement fields in lot weight history and trends; show corrected records and returned recalculated metrics and trends after accepted corrections.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned lot performance metrics, including days on feed, total weight gain, ADG, total as-fed feed consumed, FCR using as-fed pounds, feed cost of gain, and projected ship date, and refresh them after accepted feeding or weight events.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Show lot financial performance with feed cost of gain separate from available purchase and feed costs and recorded sale revenue; label broader ROI unavailable when required data is missing, and display returned feeding or sale-timing recommendations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Show operations dashboard data for active lots and pens, operational counts and inventory, ration and plan information, feed and weight performance, energy use, and lot rankings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Show a yard summary with total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost across active lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a dedicated Feed-to-Gain report comparing lots by ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, with date-range, breed, known-sex-only, and pen filters.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Allow users to export displayed or filtered Feed-to-Gain report data as CSV or PDF.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a demo and presentation view with mock operational data and materials covering the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, demo flow, coding prompts, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Make every page responsive for phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}